Meeting Minutes with HELLMANN Asia Pacific RHQ
q Meeting Form: Teleconference
q Date/Time:  13. November, 2013 09:00 =96 10:30 (HAM), 16:00-17:30 (HKG)
q Attendees:
                Hellmann

Jens Pottschul (VP Seafreight Asia, AP RHQ HKG),

Brian Tse (Seafreight Development Manager AEW, AP RHQ HKG),

Raymond  (Seafreight Development Manager AEW TP, AP RHQ HKG),

Cecilia Chen (Manager, Sea freight, Asia Pacific, Tender Management & Intra=
 Asia/Middle East Trade Management),

Sebastien Willemse (Trade Manager - Seafreight - Latin America Trade Hellma=
nn Worldwide Logistics Asia Regional Headquarters, Hong Kong)
                HJS
ASM: JS Yoon(ASM), Veronica Zhang, ASI: Alex Fan(IAS HWL pricing)
WCG: Alan Tay(WCG), Jess Yam(WCM)
UCG : Marcus Field(UCG), Soja Bong (HWL PIC)
HKGBB: KS Kim (BBS), Bernard T.W Chung
q Discussion

  1.  Performance Review

1)      Over all Export Asia

=B7         In 2013, performance increased by 16% Y-O-Y with Hanjin, wherea=
s Hellmann grew by 23% in Asia Export. HWL growth rate in Intra Asia is 40%=
, Oceania 25% and South America 40%.

=B7         70% of total HWL is from China, where Hanjin shows 55% share.

=B7         HWL itself had not much growth in Transpacific EB. Especially w=
ith Hanjin, there is no development for last 7 years.

=B7         In 2013, biggest increase is from Asia Europe Westbound by 30% =
with Hanjin, but North America and Intra Asia figures don=92t show developm=
ent.

=B7         Ideal share of origin S.E. Asia will be 10%. Hanjin has current=
ly 6%. Hanjin Singapore RHQ is very active, which can lead more BIZ opportu=
nities.



2)      Asia Europe Westbound

=B7         30% increase in 2013 with Hanjin, which is very satisfying

=B7         pExpected to grow more winning some more NAC like Gerry Weber.

=B7         Diversification of destination is important for further growth.=
 Target destination will be UK next year.

=B7         Increase to West MED is difficult due to low rates from competi=
tors. Hanjin is also trying to follow the Market, especially for Spain. Imp=
rovement will come.

=B7         Origin wise, there is potential to grow more from S.E .Asia.   =
HWL total S.E Asia share is 26%, whilst its share in Hanjin is 10%. Most of=
 BIZ is annual tender BIZ. Hanjin can participate on this, when tenders sta=
rt again.



3)      Intra Asia,  Asia to Middle East & Oceania

=B7         IAS: Biggest obstacle for Hellmann is decentralized Hanjin pric=
ing. Hellmann contact points are currently just in HKG and SYD. Cecilia nee=
ds direct contact person in RHQ level, who can send regular FAK rate update=
s and coordinate tender inquiries. This request is accepted.  Hanjin will a=
ssign contact person for Cecilia and send FAK rate whenever it changes.

=B7         Oceania is developing well with 416.7% attainment vs. target in=
 2013. Hanjin is trying to improve SVC in this area, especially New Zealand=
.  Further growth will be possible, based on SVC improvement.

=B7         Middle East: HWL grew by 25%.



4)      Transpacific EB

=B7         Even though HWL itself didn=92t grow that much in this trade,  =
no growth with Hanjin for last 7 years is not understandable as a core carr=
ier.

=B7         Main problems to support Hanjin are High Rate with at least USD=
 100/FEU rate gap, late Rate Response Time. Average 4 hours Rate Response w=
ill be reasonable. Some Carriers have Hotline for rate quotation, which giv=
es workable rate within 2 hours

=B7         Target for Jost Hellmann(Owner of HWL) in 2014 is Transpacific =
increase



5)      Asia  to Latin America

=B7         Mexico is big market with 25% share

=B7         Long term validity is the key for more BIZ development(3/6 Mont=
hs, or 1 year)

=B7         There is over charge issue from Hanjin Agency in Latin America.=
 This should be reviewed

=B7         Hanjin has intention to develop long term BIZ to West coast of =
South America to prepare for the capacity increase.  To East Coast, there i=
s no plan to expand.


2.       2014 Target: TPE target will be 4000TEU, which is same target like=
 2013. Intra Asia 600TEU & Asia to Oceania SB 900TEU could be challenging, =
but possible.  Target review will be finalized till the end of November.

q Action items
      =B7         UCG: Submit target 2014 to HWL after reviewing Middle Eas=
t figures.

=B7         ASM: Checkg the Latin America Over Charging case.

=B7         ASM, WCG: Settle regular communication with Cecilia Chen for In=
tra Asia, Middle East and Oceania. Alex Fan will be responsible for China &=
 North Asia and Jess Yam for S.E Asia and IPBC.

=B7         CCA : Review current Rate Response time and find improvement.



Meeting material is in attachment.



Best Regard



Soja Bong

+49 40 37685 580



